data.content:
I have built a 3-question quiz about computer languages using a React-style component structure. The implementation includes:

*   **React Components**: Used functional components (`Quiz` and `CheckboxGroup`) with hooks for state management.
*   **Accessible Design**:
    *   Used semantic `<fieldset>` and `<legend>` for question grouping.
    *   Associated help text with `aria-describedby`.
    *   Included a "Skip to main content" link.
    *   Ensured high contrast for the dark theme and visible focus indicators.
*   **Visual Style**: A polished dark theme using a surface-color approach with primary accent colors.
*   **Requirements**: Each question allows multiple selections, is wrapped in a `.form-field` div, and the first question includes descriptive help text.

The solution is split into `index.html`, `style.css`, and `script.js`.

### index.html
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Computer Languages Quiz</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
    <!-- React and Babel CDNs -->
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/react@18/umd/react.development.js" crossorigin></script>
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/react-dom@18/umd/react-dom.development.js" crossorigin></script>
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/@babel/standalone/babel.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
    <a href="#root" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>
    <main id="root"></main>
    <script type="text/babel" src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

